  <section|Definitions and exact finite formulas><label|definitions-and-exact-finite-formulas>

  The coefficient order is <verbatim|(scalar, diagonal first contraction,
  diagonal total contraction, off-diagonal shear)> as in
  <verbatim|YM.StressFlux.Coeff> and <verbatim|YM.StressFlux.stress>
  (<verbatim|Lean/YM/Push/STRESS_FLUX/Polynomial.lean>). The point response
  is <verbatim|YM.StressFlux.signal>; its exact Wick formula is
  <verbatim|YM.StressFlux.signal_formula>. The Green normalization is
  <verbatim|Maxwell.normal=(4\<pi\>\<twosuperior\>)\<#207B\>\<onesuperior\>>
  in <verbatim|Lean/YM/Push/MAXWELL/PotentialKernel.lean>. The scalar skim is
  <verbatim|YM.StressFlux.Line.skim>, which
  <verbatim|YM.Further.PhysicalPeriodLimitF933.skim_formula> identifies as
  the real one-point average of the <verbatim|00> entry. It is not the tensor
  trace.

  The manuscript calculations are reorganized from the actual source
  equations, not an external continuum tensor-classification result. In
  particular, it uses the explicit <verbatim|YM.StressFlux.leg0_value>,
  <verbatim|.leg1_value>, <verbatim|.leg1_cycle>, <verbatim|.sum_legs0>, and
  <verbatim|.sum_legs1> radial-potential formulas; it does not assume free
  curvature and derivative coordinates are independent. No external citation
  was located or required for these finite sums. The quotient projection has
  a source-built equivariant section; the argument does not presume its
  surjectivity without that source construction.

  <section|Open obligations and evidence><label|open-obligations-and-evidence>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Interacting-center dimension equivalence and the optical comparison
    remain in <verbatim|trace-calibration-producer.tex> as separate
    selected-source obligations; this unit proves the free reference rank
    only.

    <item>The finite raw-space classification is derived from the source's
    low-degree monomial decomposition, color invariance, signed parity, pair
    antisymmetry, and the radial <verbatim|leg1> cycle relation. The source
    reconstruction identities <verbatim|YM.StressFlux.sum_legs0> and
    <verbatim|.sum_legs1> justify that the sampled leg coefficients determine
    the actual jet functional; the prose uses no independent
    ambient-curvature coordinates.

    <item>Calibration in scale still requires the two correction directions
    and their convergence bounds; no scale-dependent claim is made here.

    <item>Commands run: <verbatim|rg -n> and <verbatim|sed -n> on the listed
    pinned Lean files; a short direct Python enumeration using the displayed
    Kronecker-delta formulas checked the five coefficient rows (three value
    probes and two divergence probes). Output: <verbatim|(32,64,0)>,
    <verbatim|(0,64,0)>, <verbatim|(0,0,\<minus\>16)>,
    <verbatim|(-256,-512,128)>, <verbatim|(0,-512,-128)> after factoring
    <verbatim|dim G\<centerdot\>\<nu\>\<twosuperior\>>. <verbatim|python3
    scripts/check_blueprint.py> was run and stopped because the
    coordinator-owned <verbatim|blueprint/units/YM-000026/unit.json> is
    absent in this isolated clone.

    <item>No Lean build or LaTeX build was run. No Lean source was modified.
  </itemize-minus>

